{"title":"Server FAQ","description":"Answers to common questions and problems when running a self-hosted Stirling PDF server.","unlisted":false,"space":"server","layout":"","article":"<a class=\"doc-space\" data-accent=\"server\" href=\"/Server/\"><svg class=\"icon\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"7\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"3\" y=\"14\" width=\"18\" height=\"7\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M7 6.5h.01M7 17.5h.01\"/></svg><span>Self-hosted server</span></a>\n    <h1>Server FAQ</h1>\n<h2 id=\"docker-pull-from-dockerstirlingpdfcom-fails-what-now\" class=\"anchor-heading\"><code>docker pull</code> from docker.stirlingpdf.com fails. What now?<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#docker-pull-from-dockerstirlingpdfcom-fails-what-now\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><p>Pull the same image from Docker Hub (<code>stirlingtools/stirling-pdf</code>) or GitHub (<code>ghcr.io/stirling-tools/stirling-pdf</code>) instead. See <a href=\"/Server/Install/Docker/#other-registries\">Other registries</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-do-i-turn-login-on-or-off\" class=\"anchor-heading\">How do I turn login on or off?<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#how-do-i-turn-login-on-or-off\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><p>Login is on by default. To turn it off, set this and restart:</p>\n<div class=\"tabs\" data-group=\"config-methods\" data-sync=\"true\" id=\"tabs-0\"><div class=\"tab-list\" role=\"tablist\"><button role=\"tab\" class=\"tab-btn active\" data-value=\"settings\" aria-selected=\"true\">Settings File</button><button role=\"tab\" class=\"tab-btn\" data-value=\"env\" aria-selected=\"false\">Environment Variable</button></div><div role=\"tabpanel\" class=\"tab-panel active\" data-value=\"settings\">\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><button class=\"codeblock-copy\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg></button><span class=\"codeblock-lang\">yaml</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">security</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  enableLogin</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">false</span></span></code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<div role=\"tabpanel\" class=\"tab-panel\" data-value=\"env\">\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><button class=\"codeblock-copy\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg></button><span class=\"codeblock-lang\">bash</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">SECURITY_ENABLELOGIN</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">false</span></span></code></pre></div>\n</div></div>\n<p>With login off, anyone who can reach the server can use it, and there are no users or single sign-on. See <a href=\"/Server/Security/Sign-in-and-Security/\">Sign-in and security</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-does-uploading-a-large-file-download-an-htm-file-or-fail\" class=\"anchor-heading\">Why does uploading a large file download an .htm file or fail?<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#why-does-uploading-a-large-file-download-an-htm-file-or-fail\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><p>Your reverse proxy is rejecting the upload: nginx allows 1 MB by default. Raise its body size limit and timeouts as in the <a href=\"/Server/Production/#example-nginx\">nginx example</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-does-stirling-pdf-use-so-much-memory-when-idle\" class=\"anchor-heading\">Why does Stirling PDF use so much memory when idle?<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#why-does-stirling-pdf-use-so-much-memory-when-idle\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><ul>\n<li>The Docker image sizes the Java heap from the container's memory limit, or from the host's RAM if there is no limit. Set a limit with <code>mem_limit</code> or <code>--memory</code>.</li>\n<li><code>latest-ultra-lite</code> uses the least memory.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>See <a href=\"/Server/Operations/Performance/\">Performance</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-does-my-server-make-requests-to-jsstripecom\" class=\"anchor-heading\">Why does my server make requests to js.stripe.com?<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#why-does-my-server-make-requests-to-jsstripecom\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><p>Only when an admin opens the checkout to buy a plan. No documents are sent to Stripe.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-do-i-check-the-logs\" class=\"anchor-heading\">How do I check the logs?<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#how-do-i-check-the-logs\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><p>Run <code>docker logs stirling-pdf</code>, or open the <code>logs</code> folder (the <code>/logs</code> volume in Docker). The first error usually names the cause.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-help\" class=\"anchor-heading\">Getting help<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#getting-help\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><p>Run <a href=\"/Server/Operations/Diagnostics/\">Diagnostics</a> to collect logs and settings into one archive, then see the <a href=\"/Tools/FAQ/\">FAQ</a> for where to report the problem.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"doc-source\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/Stirling-Tools/Stirling-Tools.github.io/edit/main/docs/Server/FAQ.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n        <svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M17 3a2.83 2.83 0 1 1 4 4L7.5 20.5 2 22l1.5-5.5L17 3z\"/></svg>\n        Edit this page on GitHub\n      </a>\n    </div>","toc":"<div class=\"toc-title\">On this page</div><ul><li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#docker-pull-from-dockerstirlingpdfcom-fails-what-now\">docker pull from docker.stirlingpdf.com fails. What now?</a></li>\n<li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#how-do-i-turn-login-on-or-off\">How do I turn login on or off?</a></li>\n<li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#why-does-uploading-a-large-file-download-an-htm-file-or-fail\">Why does uploading a large file download an .htm file or fail?</a></li>\n<li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#why-does-stirling-pdf-use-so-much-memory-when-idle\">Why does Stirling PDF use so much memory when idle?</a></li>\n<li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#why-does-my-server-make-requests-to-jsstripecom\">Why does my server make requests to js.stripe.com?</a></li>\n<li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#how-do-i-check-the-logs\">How do I check the logs?</a></li>\n<li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#getting-help\">Getting help</a></li></ul>","pager":"<a class=\"pager-link pager-prev\" href=\"/Server/Analytics-and-Telemetry/\">\n        <span class=\"pager-dir\">&larr; Previous</span>\n        <span class=\"pager-title\">Analytics &amp; telemetry</span>\n      </a><span></span>"}